    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4i_is_time-span_of"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4i_is_time-span_of",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67_refers_to",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "This property documents that an instance of E89 Propositional Object makes a statement about an instance of E1 CRM Entity. P67 refers to (is referred to by) has the P67.1 has type link to an instance of E55 Type. This is intended to allow a more detailed description of the type of reference. This differs from P129 is about (is subject of), which describes the primary subject or subjects of the instance of E89 Propositional Object."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E89_Propositional_Object"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "pt",
    "@value" : "referencia"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "refers to"
  }, {
    "@language" : "fr",
    "@value" : "renvoie à"
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "verweist auf"
  }, {
    "@language" : "el",
    "@value" : "αναφέρεται σε"
  }, {
    "@language" : "ru",
    "@value" : "ссылаeтся на"
  }, {
    "@language" : "zh",
    "@value" : "涉及"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E1_CRM_Entity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ]
}, {
  "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P7_took_place_at",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "This property describes the spatial location of an instance of E4 Period.\nThe related instance of E53 Place should be seen as a wider approximation of the geometric area within which the phenomena that characterise the period in question occurred, see below. P7 took place at (witnessed) does not convey any meaning other than spatial positioning (frequently on the surface of the earth). For example, the period “Révolution française” can be said to have taken place in “France in 1789”; the “Victorian” period may be said to have taken place in “Britain from 1837-1901” and its colonies, as well as other parts of Europe and North America. An instance of E4 Period can take place at multiple non-contiguous, non-overlapping locations.\nAny place where something happened includes the spatial projection of the happening given in the same geometric reference system. For instance, HMS Victory, as place of Lord Nelson's dying, includes the location of his body relative to the hull of HMS Victory at his time of death as the most precise location of his death. By the definition of P161 has spatial projection, an instance of E4 Period takes place on all its spatial projections to respective reference systems, that is, instances of E53 Place. Therefore, this property implies the more fully developed path from E4 Period through P161 has spatial projection, E53 Place, P89 falls within to E53 Place, where both places are defined in the same geometric reference system. The relation between an instance of E53 Place and its reference system can conveniently be documented via the property P157 is at rest relative to (provides reference space for).\nSomething that has happened at a given place can also be considered to have happened at a smaller place within it: for example, it is reasonable to say Caesar’s murder took place in Rome, but also on the Forum Romanum, and more precisely in the Curia. It is characteristic for different historical sources to use varying precision in such statements, without being in contradiction with each other. This may be due to lack of knowledge or to the relevance of the precision for the purpose of the statement. In information integration, the more precise statement improves the overall knowledge."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E4_Period"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "fr",
    "@value" : "a eu lieu dans"
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "fand statt in"
  }, {
    "@language" : "pt",
    "@value" : "ocorreu em"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "took place at"
  }, {
    "@language" : "el",
    "@value" : "έλαβε χώρα σε"
  }, {
    "@language" : "ru",
    "@value" : "совeршался на"
  }, {
    "@language" : "zh",
    "@value" : "发生地在"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E53_Place"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf" : [ {
